             dct:description "Cast Bronze standing image of the deity Vishnu with four arms. In his back hands, he holds his identifiable attributes (objects) of discus (wheel-shape) and conch Shell. In his front hands, he holds a mace or staff and an orb. His robes fly out from the front and back. There is a tang on the base, indicating that the figure would have been mounted on a larger base, perhaps as part of a tableau.,"@en ;
